{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"submission\": \"submission.json\",\n  \"summary\": \"Submitted a research product that records the exploration's observed difference in the map.\\n\\nContext from the index: three findings are confirmed_in_scope, the restart check is accepted as a bounded negative, map v11 is the accepted basis, audit units are exhausted, and the corrected exploration completed successfully (exit 0).\\n\\nObserved by that exploration: while the node ran, the same AppendEntries heartbeat handed to Raft.processHeartbeat was answered immediately (responded true, nil error, same-millisecond, node state Follower); after a clean Raft.Shutdown the identical call returned without answering inside the 500 ms observation window (responded false, node state Shutdown). The earlier build failure of the same exploration was a harness defect — the RPC response channel is send-only on the target struct — and was repaired before the recorded run.\\n\\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with the updated map.json):\\n- b-follower-append replaces its shutdown residual with the observed relationship (the branch drops the request instead of responding) and keeps the unchanged paired-transition question about the non-atomic (setState, setCurrentTerm) sequence; a preserves statement covers the confirmed findings and saved candidates that rest on this behavior.\\n- surface:Raft.processHeartbeat now states the observed consequence in its reason alongside the fast-path description, so the settled question and the unsettled one are distinguishable.\\n\\nThe feedback records the measured pair, notes the repaired build failure, and names the independent question that remains: whether the unanswered heartbeat during shutdown produces an observable cost on a real transport (for example a connection goroutine waiting on the response) is not established, since only in-process handler behaviour was observed.\\n\\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the final map version remain with the controller.\"\n}"}}
